Check the strings and the cell sequences of a state blob before their use
Fold-into: upstream/llama-context

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- A damaged state blob sizes one allocation of up to 4 GiB.

  llama_io_read_i::read_string reads a 32-bit size from the blob and allocates a buffer of that
  size before it reads the string. A full state blob of 115 bytes with a damaged size of the
  architecture name thus allocates 4 GiB, and then fails at the end of the input.

  The change: read_string reads the string in chunks of 4 KiB, thus a damaged size fails at the
  end of the input after an allocation of at most the size of the input.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--state-string-size.

- A damaged full KV state gives one cell a sequence two times, or a sequence of a different stream.

  The whole-cache path of llama_kv_cache::state_read_meta adds each sequence id of a cell with
  seq_add, which asserts that the cell does not hold the sequence (a debug build stops), and which
  counts the position two times in a release build. A sequence id of a different stream (with
  kv_unified = false) gives a stream cells that its sequence map does not know.

  The change: The read refuses a cell that gives a sequence two times or a sequence of a
  different stream, as it refuses a sequence id out of range.

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--state-cell-seq-twice.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

Files:
    src/llama-io.cpp
    src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
--- a/src/llama-io.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-io.cpp
@@ -13,8 +13,14 @@ void llama_io_read_i::read_string(std::string & str) {
     uint32_t str_size;
     read(&str_size, sizeof(str_size));
 
-    std::vector<char> buf(str_size);
-    read(buf.data(), str_size);
-
-    str.assign(buf.data(), str_size);
+    // Read in chunks: a size from a damaged state blob then fails at the end of the input, and it
+    // does not size one allocation of up to 4 GiB first. O(str_size).
+    str.clear();
+    char chunk[4096];
+    for (uint32_t left = str_size; left > 0; ) {
+        const uint32_t n = left < (uint32_t) sizeof(chunk) ? left : (uint32_t) sizeof(chunk);
+        read(chunk, n);
+        str.append(chunk, n);
+        left -= n;
+    }
 }
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
@@ -2496,6 +2496,15 @@ bool llama_kv_cache::state_read_meta(llama_io_read_i & io, uint32_t strm, uint32
                     return false;
                 }
 
+                // A cell holds each sequence one time, and a sequence has its cells in its own stream
+                // only. A damaged blob can give a sequence two times, or a sequence of a different
+                // stream: seq_add would then count the position two times (an assert in a debug
+                // build), or a stream would hold cells that its sequence map does not know.
+                if (cells.seq_has(i, seq_id) || seq_to_stream[seq_id] != strm) {
+                    LLAMA_LOG_ERROR("%s: cell %u gives the seq_id %d two times or in the wrong stream\n", __func__, i, seq_id);
+                    return false;
+                }
+
                 cells.seq_add(i, seq_id);
             }
         }
